CORE
main.c
--datarace --no-assertions --no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 2
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^BDD prune: removed 1 shared accesses with a contradictory guard
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The thread writes g only under b && !b, b = (c & 1), through two separately
named guards, so the expression simplifier keeps the write; as BDDs the guard
is false and the write is removed before the encoding. (With plain c the path
bounds in symex already decide !c false and the write never reaches the BDDs.)
